```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: green
REAL_USE_CASE: LLM training-data pipeline engineers, privacy/compliance teams, and eval-contamination auditors who dedupe multilingual web corpora (especially CJK, German, French) before model training. Needed when the model tokenizer normalizes via NFKC+casefold (the pervasive multilingual default) but the production deduper runs NFD+lowercase (e.g., datatrove simplify_text), creating a hidden class of model-identical duplicates that escape removal.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Real win, not microbenchmark-only. On REAL allenai/c4 multilingual validation (20,000 docs, 5 languages), residual_FN_rate = 95.1% (8,605 / 9,044 model-identical NFKC-twin pairs escape production dedup). Per-language: zh 99.8%, ja 98.4%, de 94.7%, fr 94.6%, ar 55.6%. Prevalence: 45.2% of docs have a distinct model-identical twin (ja 90%, zh 83%). Drivers are real-world compatibility characters: fullwidth ASCII 300,261 chars (pervasive in CJK web), plus German ß→ss, ligatures, enclosed/circled, super/subscripts. Robustness: 34.6% of residual FNs survive production 5-gram char-shingle MinHash at T=0.8 (58.7% word-token), confirming the gap is not an exact-string artifact. The divergence is structural per Unicode: NFD is canonical-only and by spec cannot collapse compatibility characters; NFKC+casefold is required to match the model.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [1] Code change in dedup libraries (datatrove, internal pipelines) to replace NFD+lower with NFKC+casefold; [2] Reprocessing of existing deduped datasets to close the 95% exposure; [3] Awareness/training for data engineers (the seam is verified open in >=2 codebases per committee#1, indicating current practice misses it); [4] Validation that aligning to the model's normalizer does not collapse intended distinctions (safe because the model already collapses these classes; the fix aligns deduper to model behavior, not vice-versa). Barrier is low: the fix is a one-line normalizer swap, not a new algorithm, and runtime cost of NFKC+casefold is negligible versus shingling/MinHash.
RATIONALE: L1 EXP-0069 measured residual_FN_rate = 95.1% (8,605 / 9,044) on real C4 multilingual, exceeding the committee#1 GREEN gate (>=1%) by 95x. Every language clears the gate by >=55x. The mechanism (NFKC+casefold vs NFD+lower) was proven in L0 EXP-0068 (FN=1.00 when deduper weaker, FN=0.00 when aligned, with matched-edit-distance typo control). Committee#1 verified the seam is genuinely open in >=2 codebases and found no fatal prior-art collision. The finding is actionable: production dedupers currently do not use NFKC (verified), and the 95% hidden model-identical duplicate exposure is currently real, affecting memorization, privacy, and eval-contamination risk in multilingual training.
```
